WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.320
Priya: Okay, Alex. Walk me through the app side. Anything weird in the logs?

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:10.848
Alex: Everything looks normal. The requests just don't arrive.

3
00:00:10.848 --> 00:00:13.992
Priya: So it's upstream of us, then.

4
00:00:13.992 --> 00:00:18.143
Dan: Yeah. I'll pull the load balancer metrics.

5
00:00:18.143 --> 00:00:22.799
Priya: Thanks. Any connection resets on the way in?

6
00:00:22.799 --> 00:00:26.591
Dan: Hang on... yes. A lot of them.

7
00:00:26.591 --> 00:00:29.999
Sam: Let me tail the log on the edge box.

8
00:00:29.999 --> 00:00:34.943
Priya: Do one thing, Sam — filter for 502 only.

9
00:00:34.943 --> 00:00:38.639
Sam: Will do. That cuts the noise.

10
00:00:38.639 --> 00:00:43.175
Dan: Okay, so the 502s are all coming from one AZ.

11
00:00:43.175 --> 00:00:46.366
Priya: Interesting. Which one?

12
00:00:46.366 --> 00:00:49.318
Dan: The one we moved traffic to yesterday.

13
00:00:49.318 --> 00:00:54.838
Priya: Right. So this is a network thing, not an app thing.

14
00:00:54.838 --> 00:00:59.230
Sam: Agreed. I'll keep watching the error rate.

